.TH CENTRAL-AUDIO 1 "November 2026" "central-audio 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
central-audio \- inspect and control audio devices with a GTK2 interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B central-audio
.br
.B central-audio --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B central-audio
lists sources and sinks on a running PulseAudio-compatible server.
It offers controls for default devices, volume, and restoration of saved
changes.
Changing a default device does not confirm the device selected in an
already running browser call.
.PP
Android microphone capture is optional and requires an external
scrcpy version 2.3 or later, FFmpeg with PulseAudio output support, and adb.
The application does not bundle these programs or a web browser.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the application version without opening the graphical interface.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/central-gtk2-audio/
Private application state. When XDG_STATE_HOME is unset, the base directory
is the user's .local/state directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pactl (1),
.BR scrcpy (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR adb (1)
.SH AUTHORS
central-audio-bluetooth-android-linux contributors.
